 ## Overview
-Energy Region Compositing is a volume rendering technique that composites multiple energy-specific volumes within a specific region of interest defined by a magnitude volume [S1, unofficial]. It applies a threshold to energy intensity before compositing, blending colors based on normalized intensities above that threshold [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard direct volume ray casting which integrates opacity and color along a single scalar field, this method selectively renders energy contributions only where the magnitude volume indicates presence, effectively masking out background noise or irrelevant regions [S1, unofficial].
